※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4615 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_GIVEN_BACK

※ Each arm gives `x` something made in a different arena, so after the `if` it may hold
※ either: what it was made in is the union of what the arms that reach the join left.  Emptying
※ one of the two kills it.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let s1: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let s2: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(s2)
    let c: bool = true
    let x: mut str = "-"
    if c:
        x ← "a" ⧺ "b" in s1
    else:
        x ← "c" ⧺ "d" in s2
    ⎕empty(s1)
    if x = "ab": 0u6 else: 1u6
